  "implementation": {
    "shared_projection": "The same bounded SQL projection is used by both readers. Newly exposed SQL reservation_id is returned only for exact TEXT/48-byte values; oversized/non-text IDs become NULL and fail identity comparison.",
    "shared_validator": "_reservation_row(row8, permit) compares SQL reservation_id/scope/task/slot/permit canonical bytes, then retains the exact prior state/ref/terminal-presence checks and returns the original seven-column tuple.",
    "point_lookup": "_reservation still looks up exactly the requested primary key, requires exactly one row, and uses the shared pure validator.",
    "totals": "_totals uses one scope-filtered ordered SELECT and iterates its cursor. It validates every captured permit and row, accumulates reserved nanoseconds with exact Python integers, preserves active-slot conflict and scope/budget checks, and never re-queries by the permit's claimed ID.",
    "unchanged": "No schema/index/transaction/Stop/HOLD/recovery/lease/settlement/refund changes. No SQL SUM, floating aggregation, cache, fetchall of history, new runner, or audit-row skipping. Ingress and IdeaLake are outside this author's edits."
  },
